tinyq
=====

[![build status](https://ci.example.com/badge.svg)](https://ci.example.com/tinyq) [![license](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

A tiny job queue on top of SQLite — no broker, no daemon.

Install
-------

```
pip install tinyq
tinyq init --db jobs.sqlite
```

Usage
-----

```
from tinyq import Queue

q = Queue("jobs.sqlite")
q.put({"to": "ana@example.com"})
```

Roadmap
-------

* retries with backoff
* priorities
* a list item with `` `backticks` `` and ``` ``double`` ``` inside code
* snake\_case\_names and \*stars\* in text, 2 \* 3 = 6

Use the `__init__` hook, or set `TINYQ_DB=/var/lib/tinyq.db`.

```
  indented
    pre block
```

```
one leading newline
```
-- end
