-- page | wiki.html | default
**Paxos** is a family of protocols for solving
[consensus](/wiki/Consensus_(computer_science) "Consensus (computer science)")
in a network of unreliable processors.[[1]](#cite_note-1)
It was first submitted in 1989.[[2]](#cite_note-2)

Contents
--------

* [1 History](#History)
* [2 Basic Paxos](#Basic_Paxos)
  + [2.1 Phase 1](#Phase_1)

History
-------

The topic predates the protocol. In 1988, Lynch, Dwork and Stockmeyer had demonstrated
the solvability of consensus in a broad family of "partially synchronous" systems.

Basic Paxos
-----------

### Phase 1

Prepare
:   A *Proposer* creates a message, which we call a "Prepare", identified with a number *n*.

Promise
:   An *Acceptor* waits for a *Prepare* message.

1. **[^](#cite_ref-1)** Lamport, Leslie (1998).
2. **[^](#cite_ref-2)** Lamport, Leslie (2001). *Paxos Made Simple*.
-- end
-- page | wiki.html | atx
